  "components": [],
  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What happens now",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Two things about sorting on the Sales By Customer report do not match the written description."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "One: every column heading can be clicked to sort except two - the little arrow column at the far left, which is correct, and the Location column, which is not. Location has no sort arrow and clicking it does nothing. The server itself can sort by location perfectly well, so this is only missing from the screen."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Two: rows with no value in them sort to the wrong end. Sorting Margin % smallest-first puts all the blank ones at the TOP, and largest-first puts them at the BOTTOM. The written description asks for the exact opposite."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "How to see it",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Open Reports, then Sales By Customer, and choose This Year so there are plenty of rows."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Click each column heading in turn. Every one sorts except Location, which has no arrow and does not respond."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Click Margin % once (smallest first). The first rows shown have a dash instead of a percentage. Click again (largest first) and the dashes have moved to the end."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What should happen instead",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Location should sort like every other column. Blank values should go to the bottom when sorting smallest-first and to the top when sorting largest-first."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What we tested it on",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "QA branch sv8582, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026. Date range This Year (1 January to 6 August 2026), both locations, Product Type Parts & Service, 384 customers in the set. 19 of the first 30 rows had no Margin % value."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "How bad is it",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Low. Sorting works on the other twelve columns and the order it produces is correct; it is the blank rows that end up in the wrong place, and one column that cannot be sorted at all."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "What we ruled out",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "We checked the sort is genuinely applied and not a stale screen: each click sends a fresh request and the first page comes back in the new order, and the heading itself reports which way it is sorted. We also confirmed the server accepts a sort by location and answers correctly, so the gap is on the screen only."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Sales By Customer report specification, version 15, requirement S10-R1, which says: \"Every column is sortable except the chevron column.\"."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Sales By Customer report specification, version 15, requirement S10-R3, which says: \"A missing value sorts to the bottom in ascending order and to the top in descending order; a Margin % em-dash cell counts as a missing value.\"."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "That is source type 2: the specification (PRD) in Confluence. The version number given is the Confluence page version, not the version written inside the page."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
